lynxcc — Lynx Game Development SDK
==================================

This distribution is multi-licensed. Different components carry different
licenses; this file is the authoritative copy of the cc65 zlib-style package
license that forms the baseline, and it points to the other licenses that layer
on top of it. The complete, human-readable inventory of every notice in the
distribution lives in doc/licenses.html, and the per-component policy is
recorded in design/LYNX_LICENSE_POLICY_DESIGN.md.

  - Package baseline (cc65) — the zlib-style permissive license reproduced
    below. It covers the inherited cc65 toolchain, runtime and library sources,
    including the static TGI graphics modules and the ComLynx serial modules
    that were extracted from Karri Kaksonen's cc65 drivers (each such file keeps
    its own copyright line and an extraction note pointing here). Bundled
    third-party decompression code (include/lynx/zlib.h, include/lynx/lz4.h and
    their libraries/compress/ sources) is provided under the same zlib-style
    terms and additionally carries its own upstream notice.

  - Fork-authored sources — files this fork wrote from scratch are licensed
    under the Mozilla Public License 2.0 (MPL-2.0). The full text is in
    LICENSE-MPL-2.0.txt, and each covered file carries an SPDX-License-Identifier
    header.

  - examples/ and templates/ — licensed under the MIT License (a LICENSE file
    in each directory) so you can copy starter code into your own Atari Lynx
    games with no copyleft reach.

  - Documentation (doc/, design/) — licensed under Creative Commons Attribution
    4.0 International (CC-BY-4.0). The full legal code is in doc/LICENSE.

Every source file carries an SPDX-License-Identifier tag identifying which of
the above applies to it. Where a documentation page reproduces a third party's
license verbatim, that quoted text remains under its own terms.


